{
  "version": 1,
  "goal": "Read-only parity audit of ui/** against original Orca renderer, ORCA_LITE_FIX_PLAN.md, and PERF_NOTES.md, with complete classification across shell/UX, shortcuts, settings, and code-level plan conformance.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "title": "Read the design-plan acceptance criteria, Phases 2/6/7/8 frontend requirements, PERF_NOTES.md, and current ui/src structure without modifying files.",
      "status": "done",
      "note": "Read ORCA_LITE_FIX_PLAN.md Phase 2 completion/model, Phases 6/7/8, React UI acceptance/DoD; read PERF_NOTES.md; enumerated ui/src tree. No repository writes."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "title": "Audit shell/UX fidelity against original-dist assets: sidebar, worktree cards, tab bar, split panes, states, design tokens/typography, resize and divider behavior.",
      "status": "done",
      "note": "Audited shell/sidebar/worktree/tab/split/states/tokens/typography against original WorktreeCard, useSidebarResize, I18nProvider CSS, App worktree list and split-resize CSS. Found fixed/inert sidebar controls, missing split resize handle, and undefined semantic Tailwind tokens/system font divergence; core worktree/tab/split shell exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "title": "Enumerate every keyboard handler in ui/src and every relevant original shortcut family/keybinding; classify each family as parity, by-design gap, or defect.",
      "status": "done",
      "note": "Enumerated ui/src keyboard handlers: only TabBar.tsx onKeyDown Enter/Space close handler; no keydown/metaKey/ctrlKey/custom xterm shortcut handlers elsewhere. Audited original agent-tab, editor-shortcuts, terminal-shortcut-policy, shortcut-platform, ShortcutKeyCombo, useShortcutLabel and manifest bindings; terminal/tab shortcut families are missing, editor/agent/browser families map to explicit design gaps."
    },
    {
      "id": "T4",
      "title": "Audit settings/preferences surfaces in original-dist and orca-lite; classify functionality and gaps against the explicit by-design gap list and plan scope.",
      "status": "done",
      "note": "Original Settings surface audited via Settings-yKTVxZPa.js and useSettingsNavigationMetadata: General, Integrations, Git, Terminal, Appearance, Input, Notifications, Shortcuts, Stats, SSH/remote, browser/mobile/orchestration/etc. Lite exposes only Sidebar Settings IconButton with no onClick and has no settings component/routes. Unsupported browser/editor/remote/automation/orchestration settings are explicit by-design gaps; terminal/appearance/shortcut settings and the exposed inert Settings affordance are not gap-exempt."
    },
    {
      "id": "T5",
      "title": "Audit code-level plan conformance: listener timing, UTF-8/base64 streaming, session/tab/pane separation, LayoutState reducer, tauri invoke boundary, DTO casing, structured errors, sample agents, lazy terminal bundle, WebGL lifecycle.",
      "status": "done",
      "note": "Plan conformance audited. Passes: terminal listeners are ensured before spawn; Rust base64 + per-session streaming TextDecoder; TerminalSession/Tab/Pane separation with renderer-only TerminalPane; reducer invariants; Tauri invoke isolated to lib/tauri.ts; Rust/TS camelCase; code-based structured error mapping; lazy xterm/Fit/CSS and lazy WebGL with lifecycle counters/fallback. Deviations: worktree_changed only carries create/delete variants vs Phase 6.1 dirty/lock/prune/branch requirements; selectAgents synthesizes every terminal tab as an ActiveAgent rather than identifying actual agent sessions, despite eliminating hardcoded names."
    },
    {
      "id": "T6",
      "title": "Re-open the five most load-bearing citations, verify all table citations are grep-verifiable, inspect git status/diff read-only, and complete the authoritative completion check.",
      "status": "done",
      "note": "Re-opened and re-validated five load-bearing citations: ORCA_LITE_FIX_PLAN.md Phase 6/7; Sidebar.tsx inert/fixed affordances; workspaceStore.ts listener-before-spawn/model ownership; terminalEvents.ts singleton listener/decode bus; original terminal-shortcut-policy actions. Inspected current ui staged diff read-only; no repository changes were made by this audit."
    }
  ],
  "created_ms": 1787272369492,
  "updated_ms": 1787273260332,
  "verifications": []
}
